Spec: Invoice Repository

Platform: Python 3

Purpose:
  Store invoices in memory for the fixture service.

Structure:
  ./repository.py: Repository implementation.
  ./models.py: Stored invoice model.
  ./service.py: Repository caller.

Owns:
  ./repository.py
  ./repository.sdd

Can modify:
  ./repository.py
  ./repository.sdd

Can read:
  ./models.py
  ./service.py
  ../../tests/test_service.py

Must:
  Save invoices by invoice id.
  Return None for missing invoice ids.
  Return customer invoice lists without exposing internal storage.
  Stay in memory for the fixture.

Must not:
  Add filesystem persistence.
  Add database clients or network dependencies.

Depends on:
  @invoice_demo.models.Invoice

Scenario: saved invoices can be queried
  Given @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository.save stores an invoice
  When @invoice_demo.repository.InvoiceRepository.get receives the same id
  Then it returns the saved invoice

Example:
  implementation: ./repository.py
  behavior test: ../../tests/test_service.py
